# CODEOWNERS — who must approve a change before it can be merged into `main`.
#
# The effective rule is:
#   * anyone (including people with no access to this repository) may open a
#     pull request — they just fork the repository;
#   * a pull request can only be merged once it has been approved by the
#     required number of reviewers WITH WRITE ACCESS;
#   * with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled on the branch protection
#     rule for `main`, the required approval must come from someone listed in
#     THIS FILE. An approval from any other collaborator does not count.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING
# ------------------------
# 1. Every owner listed below MUST have "Write" access to this repository.
#    GitHub silently drops owners without it: "If you specify a user or team
#    that doesn't exist or has insufficient access, a code owner will not be
#    assigned."
# 2. This file is read from the BASE branch of a pull request, so it only takes
#    effect after it is merged into `main`.
# 3. Turning on branch protection alone is not enough — the option
#    "Require review from Code Owners" must also be enabled on the `main`
#    branch protection rule.
# 4. An approval from ANY ONE of the owners listed for a path is enough; "all
#    of them" is not required.

# Everything in the repository needs an approval from the maintainers.
# ALL THREE must keep "Write" access, otherwise GitHub drops them from the list
# and their approval stops counting. Remove a name here to revoke that person's
# ability to unblock a pull request (they may still be a collaborator).
#   @hoymiles-ha  repository owner (admin)
#   @ls199303     maintainer      (write)
#   @AidenZL      maintainer      (write)
*                           @hoymiles-ha   @ls199303   @AidenZL

